# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# hybrid-ai :: hardened .gitignore
#
# WHAT THIS FILE DOES
# Git will refuse to track any file matching a pattern below. Every entry here
# is a security control, not a tidiness preference. Two categories matter most:
#
#   1. Secrets   -- .env holds live API keys. Committing it once means rotating
#                   every credential it contained, because git history is
#                   forever.
#   2. Local state -- ollama_data/ and webui_data/ hold your models, chat
#                   history, and vector database. These are large, machine
#                   specific, and must never be overwritten by a git pull.
#
# If you add a new file that holds credentials, add it here FIRST.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Secrets / environment -------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.key
*.pem
*.crt
*.p12
*.pfx
*_rsa
*_ed25519
authkey*
runtime.env

# --- Backup working state ---------------------------------------------------
# Staging holds PLAINTEXT database snapshots while a backup runs, and the
# restore/safety directories hold recovered copies of everything. None of it
# belongs in git.
.backup-staging/
.restore-work/
.restore-test-*/
webui_data.pre-restore-*/
backup.log

# --- Persistent local state (your knowledge base - NEVER commit) -----------
ollama_data/
webui_data/
chroma_data/
mnt/
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db

# --- Diagnostic bundles -----------------------------------------------------
# Generated by collect-diagnostics.sh. Redacted, but they still describe your
# environment in detail and have no business in a repository.
diagnostics-*.txt
hybrid-ai-diagnostic-*.txt

# --- Logs ------------------------------------------------------------------
# install.log and the pod event log hold deployment metadata (never secrets),
# but they describe your environment and have no business in a public repo.
*.log
install.log
logs/
nohup.out

# --- Python ----------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.venv/
venv/
env/
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/

# --- Editors / OS ----------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~

# --- Docker / build artifacts ---------------------------------------------
docker-compose.override.yml
*.tar
*.tar.gz
